  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ReadDictionary",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/ipc/reader.cc",
    "description": "ReadDictionary calls internal::SwapEndianArrayData() on dictionary ArrayData parsed from untrusted IPC metadata when swap_endian is enabled, without validating that buffer sizes are consistent with the declared logical length/type layout. In ArrayDataEndianSwapper::Visit(const MonthDayNanoIntervalType&) (arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/util.cc:210), the loop uses data_->length to index reinterpret_cast MonthDayNanos elements from buffers[1], causing out-of-bounds read when length is larger than the actual value buffer size.",
    "conditions": "The PoV must produce an IPC stream with schema endianness different from native (so context.swap_endian becomes true in schema unpacking), include a dictionary batch whose value type is MonthDayNanoInterval (or another path using unchecked length/buffer assumptions), and craft dictionary ArrayData with inconsistent metadata (large length, undersized data buffer). Data flow: fuzz input -> StreamDecoderInternal::ReadDictionary -> ReadDictionary(metadata, context, ...) -> SwapEndianArrayData(dict_data) -> ArrayDataEndianSwapper::Visit(MonthDayNanoIntervalType) OOB read."
  },
